            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "Broadcast reproduction right is a special right under Section 37 of the Copyright Act 1957 granted to every broadcasting organisation. It protects the broadcast signal from unauthorised re-broadcasting, recording, reproduction, and commercial exploitation. This right lasts 25 years from the calendar year following the broadcast."
          }
        },
        {
