          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "Section 31D allows any broadcasting organisation to communicate published literary/musical works and sound recordings by paying prescribed royalties - no separate permission from each copyright owner needed. A Pune radio station can play songs via statutory license. Compliance documentation and payment records must be maintained."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "What acts constitute infringement of broadcast rights?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "Under Section 37(3), without the broadcaster's license: re-broadcasting the broadcast, causing public hearing/viewing on payment, making sound/visual recordings, reproducing such recordings, and selling/renting recordings commercially. Civil remedies (injunction, damages) and criminal penalties (up to 3 years, Rs 2 lakh fine) available."
