            <div class="content-text">
                
                <p><strong>Copyright Act 1957, Chapter VIII (Sections 37-39A):</strong> Broadcast reproduction rights and performer's rights. Section 37 grants automatic 25-year protection for every broadcast. Source: <a href="https://www.copyright.gov.in/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">copyright.gov.in</a></p><p><strong>Section 2(dd):</strong> Broadcast = communication to public by wireless diffusion or wire, including re-broadcast.</p><p><strong>Section 31D (Statutory License):</strong> Broadcasters can use published literary/musical works and sound recordings by paying prescribed royalties.</p><p><strong>Section 39 (Coexistence):</strong> Broadcast right does not affect separate content copyright. Both layers coexist.</p><p><strong>Civil Remedies (Section 55):</strong> Injunction, damages, accounts of profits. <strong>Criminal (Section 63):</strong> 6 months to 3 years imprisonment, Rs 50,000 to Rs 2 lakh fine.</p><p><strong>Bombay High Court (Pune Bench):</strong> Jurisdiction for copyright infringement matters in Pune district. Source: <a href="https://mib.gov.in" target="_blank" rel="noopener">mib.gov.in</a></p>

